cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Where does physical knowledge belong in a surrogate? A pre-registered
  falsification ladder for MOF/COF adsorption column dynamics
message: If you use this software or its results, please cite it.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Abdulhamid
    family-names: Batayhi
    email: abdulbatayhi@gmail.com
repository-code: "https://github.com/REPLACE-ME/ai-mof-cof-dynamics"
abstract: >-
  A pre-registered falsification ladder testing seven candidate explanations for
  the transfer gap in surrogate models of MOF/COF adsorption columns: more data,
  more capacity, a richer edge basis (KAN), a PDE residual loss, operator
  learning, structural identification, and whether learning is needed at all.
  Six are eliminated. The binding constraint is measured directly — the
  parameter-to-coefficient map — and the one intervention that moves it is a
  two-wave change of coordinates that removes both front trajectories before
  projection. Includes a verified finite-difference reference solver, a
  cluster-robust calibrated inference protocol, and a public corrections ledger.
keywords:
  - metal-organic frameworks
  - covalent organic frameworks
  - atmospheric water harvesting
  - breakthrough curves
  - operator learning
  - reduced-order modelling
  - Kolmogorov n-width
  - physics-informed machine learning
  - negative results
  - pre-registration
